# Line endings are LF everywhere — in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this the repository drifts: `core.autocrlf` is false here, so git stores whatever an
# editor happened to write, and on Windows that is CRLF for some tools and LF for others. Two
# files (src/gmail.ts, SECURITY.md) had ended up CRLF while the other 79 were LF, and any diff
# touching them showed the whole file instead of the lines that changed — 2567 lines for a
# 9-line edit, with `git blame` useless for the same reason.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than `text=auto` alone: the latter normalises the repository but still checks
# out CRLF on Windows, which puts the drift right back into the next editor that rewrites a file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# There is no binary content in this repository (checked: every tracked file is text), so no
# `binary` entries are needed. Add one here before committing an image, font or bundle.
